---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Services
eyebrow: Services
subtitle: Hands-on help for people and organizations running, or planning to run, a publication on Project Broadsheet.
permalink: /services/
---
<div class="lead" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
  Project Broadsheet is free to use on your own — genuinely free, no catches. But if you'd rather have someone set it up, migrate your archive, design a bespoke brand, or handle ongoing maintenance, that's what this page is about. I take on a small number of engagements at a time, and I prefer to work with independent publishers, small organizations, and people doing work I'm proud to point at.
</div>

{% for svc in services %}
<section class="feature-block" id="{{ svc.slug }}">
  <div class="feature-block__grid">
    <header class="feature-block__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">{{ svc.name }}</span>
      <h2>{{ svc.name }}</h2>
      <p class="feature-block__summary">{{ svc.summary }}</p>
      <p class="feature-block__price"><strong>Starting at {{ svc.startingAt }}</strong></p>
      <div class="feature-block__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ svc.cta.url }}">{{ svc.cta.label }}</a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <ul class="feature-block__list">
      {% for inc in svc.includes %}<li>{{ inc }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">
  <div class="callout__title">How I work</div>
  <p>Every project starts with a conversation — usually a 30-minute call where you tell me what you're building and I tell you whether I'm the right person to help. If I'm not, I'll say so and try to point you somewhere better.</p>
  <p>Every email, quote, and reply comes from me personally. No bots, no AI, no account managers. That means responses occasionally take a day, but it means you always know who you're talking to.</p>
</div>
